                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "rule": "c0 * weight + c1 * compatible_greedy - c2 * max(0, compatible_cover - compatible_greedy) - c3 * neighbor_max_weight",
      "patch_policy": {
        "anchor": "resource_boundary",
        "destroy_count": 6,
        "patch_cap": 40,
        "expand_hops": 2,
        "reconstruction": "rcl"
      },
      "evaluation_plan": {
        "feature_scope": "patch",
        "max_feature_cpu_fraction": 0.22,
        "lazy": true
      },
      "adaptation_template": {
        "mutation_scales": [0.1, 0.35, 0.9,
          1.3],
        "stagnation_trials": 10,
        "action": "diversify"
      },
      "coefficients": [1.0, 0.6, 0.08, 0.05],
      "rationale": "Recomputing greedy completion and cover weight on the compatible residual exposes arrangements beyond the root's immediate neighborhood. Their gap is a ranking heuristic, not a certificate of conditional preference or final quality. Resource-boundary anchoring concentrates six-contact destruction on competing resource commitments, while top-three reconstruction explores alternatives. Cover queries remain within the exact 40-node patch. The zero-heavy repair traces motivate diversification after ten stagnant trials; complete feasible reward and charged CPU determine whether this operator earns credit."
    },
